Implementation of duplicate detection:
```
import yaml
def duplicates(text):
    node = yaml.compose(text)
    out=[]
    def walk(n, path):
        if isinstance(n, yaml.MappingNode):
            seen={}
            for k,v in n.value:
                key = k.value
                if key in seen:
                    out.append({"path": path+"."+key, "key": key, "lines":[seen[key], k.start_mark.line+1]})
                else:
                    seen[key]=k.start_mark.line+1
                walk(v, path+"."+key)
        elif isinstance(n, yaml.SequenceNode):
            for i,v in enumerate(n.value): walk(v, f"{path}[{i}]")
    walk(node,"")
    return out
```
Note yaml.compose can throw on duplicate anchors etc. Fine.

